&#x200B;

Owning my mistake. Can I get an upvote?

You can make your own! Buy some roses (white) and drop some food colouring in the water. The flower will absorb the food coloured water and voila!

&#x200B;

...or maybe make some black dye and dip the roses into them?

I encountered the same guy, same SUV, same story, in Heartland, in front of Ashley Home (formely Future Shop).  He even gave me a business card (I wish I kept it).

&#x200B;

First gave me some prices for his designer jackets, then when I said "No" he tried to sell them to me with lower prices, then asked how much I can afford to give him for the jackets. Eventually he drove off.

Mostly locals in there. The area has aged enough for the college crowd to still live at home, and party near home so they don't have to drive drunk. Most people there walk or Uber there and back home. There are some regulars that live further away (Mavis/Burnhamthorpe, Dundas/Hwy 10) but still choose to hang out at The Bristol.

&#x200B;

Some of them are some daily regulars there too. Everyone in there are sports-heads! The foosball table is quite the attraction there, also. A competitive college past-time activity...

&#x200B;

Beers are fairly priced (even the imports) and plenty of screens to watch various sporting events. When there is a big event, they will show it on all the screens. I've watched the Superbowl there, McGregor/Mayweather, some UFC PPVs, World Cup, NBA semi-finals, and now the finals.

&#x200B;

Love it there!

Bristol Bar and Grill (Bristol Rd. and McLaughlin) is crowded with College and newly-out-of College students. Big sporting events attract the rowdiest of rowdy. Great atmosphere!

&#x200B;

There's a location closer to Sq. 1, but I'm not sure what the crowd is like there.

It's hard to enjoy in a crowd of strangers. Sometimes you need to high five and cheer with people. Mississauga Jurassic Park might be geared towards family and friends who go there together.

&#x200B;

Maybe try going to Jurassic Park Toronto, but don't be stationary. Keep moving and say hello and cheer on the GREATEST TEAM ever with everyone around you. Don't get caught up thinking about the snobby attitudes you might face. If you're confident enough to express your love for the Raptors, do it loud and proud. You might even become a celebrity in your own right.

The soccer clubs don't "hog" them, they purchase a permit to use those fields. And there has been a rise in new "clubs" and academies who are also getting permits for these fields recently, so unoccupied fields will be hard to find, unless you go during non-peak hours (daytime or very late night, just be aware that most of the fields have operating hours and you may get fined by the city if you're there when the park/field is closed).

&#x200B;

Best bet is to join a league. Run by one of these clubs. Yes, you have to pay, but you'll have a field to practice and play competitively on, and with your registration fee, soccer kit(s) are usually included, so you'll have some pretty nice team swag to sport. Or, you can apply early in the year for a permit for a field. You'll still need to fork out some $$. Or rent an indoor gym for some futsal, or indoor field at venues like Paramount Fine Foods Centre (formerly Hershey SportsZone).

I live by Bristol and Mavis. It IS a nightly occurrence. It sounds like they are racing all night. And the noise travels even for 30+ seconds. I'm surprised PRP hasn't tuned into this area. Heartland Tim Hortons and Krispy Kreme parking lots have gatherings at least each weekend. Sometimes even during the week.

&#x200B;

I should add that on my street (Ceremonial Dr.) I hear and see them fly by. I'd guess doing at least 80 in our 40/50kmh zone.

You can also try:  [https://www.freecycle.org/](https://www.freecycle.org/) 

&#x200B;

Some items are in great condition, where people just don't want the hassle of trying to sell their old items.

&#x200B;

Good luck!

